"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"functions-api\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Qiskit Functions access on an instance {#configure-qiskit-functions-access-on-an-instance}"
msgstr "Configurare l'accesso a Qiskit Functions su un'istanza {#configure-qiskit-functions-access-on-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use these instructions to configure Qiskit Functions access on an existing IBM Quantum Compute Service instance by using the IBM Cloud Resource Controller API.  Follow the instructions in order, as the commands build on each other.  For example, variables such as the token and URL are set in one step and reused in later steps. \n"
msgstr "Usa queste istruzioni per configurare l'accesso a Qiskit Functions su un'istanza IBM Quantum Compute Service esistente utilizzando l'API IBM Cloud Resource Controller. Segui le istruzioni in ordine, poiché i comandi si basano l'uno sull'altro. Ad esempio, variabili come il token e l'URL vengono impostate in un passaggio e riutilizzate nei passaggi successivi. \n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites {#prerequisites}"
msgstr "Prerequisiti {#prerequisites}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An IBM Cloud API key (also called a token).  If necessary, create your API key on the [dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com). \n"
msgstr "Una chiave API IBM Cloud (chiamata anche token). Se necessario, crea la tua chiave API sulla [dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com). \n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CRN of the instance you want to configure.  The instance's CRN is listed on your [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.\n"
msgstr "Il CRN dell'istanza che vuoi configurare. Il CRN dell'istanza è elencato nella tua pagina [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Get a bearer token {#step-1-get-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr "Passaggio 1: ottenere un bearer token {#step-1-get-a-bearer-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exchange your API key for a bearer token. You will pass this token in the authorization header of all resource controller requests. Run the following code to generate a bearer token:\n"
msgstr "Scambia la tua chiave API con un bearer token. Passerai questo token nell'intestazione di autorizzazione di tutte le richieste a Resource Controller. Esegui il seguente codice per generare un bearer token:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request POST \\\n"
"  --url 'https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token' \\\n"
"  --header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \\\n"
"  --data 'apikey=<YOUR_API_KEY>&grant_type=urn%3Aibm%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Aapikey'\n"
"  --silent | jq .\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"import requests\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "api_key = \"<YOUR_API_KEY>\"\n"
msgstr "api_key = \"<YOUR_API_KEY>\"\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.post(\n"
"    \"https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token\",\n"
"    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"},\n"
"    params={\n"
"        \"apikey\": api_key,\n"
"        \"grant_type\": \"urn:ibm:params:oauth:grant-type:apikey\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"token = resp.json()[\"access_token\"]\n"
"print(token) \n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.post(\n"
"    \"https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token\",\n"
"    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"},\n"
"    params={\n"
"        \"apikey\": api_key,\n"
"        \"grant_type\": \"urn:ibm:params:oauth:grant-type:apikey\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"token = resp.json()[\"access_token\"]\n"
"print(token) \n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The response includes an `access_token` field, which is your bearer token. Copy this value.\n"
msgstr "La risposta include un campo `access_token`, che è il tuo bearer token. Copia questo valore.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Verify access {#step-2-verify-access}"
msgstr "Passaggio 2: verificare l'accesso {#step-2-verify-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before making any changes, confirm that your token works and inspect the current instance configuration.\n"
msgstr "Prima di apportare modifiche, conferma che il tuo token funzioni e ispeziona la configurazione attuale dell'istanza.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"The CRN must be manually URL-encoded in the path. Replace each `:` with `%3A` and each `/` with `%2F`. For example, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` becomes `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Importante\">\n"
"Il CRN deve essere codificato manualmente per URL nel percorso. Sostituisci ogni `:` con `%3A` e ogni `/` con `%2F`. Ad esempio, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` diventa `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"import urllib.parse\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
msgstr "crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CRN will be URL-encoded into the path."
msgstr "Il CRN verrà codificato per URL nel percorso."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"instance_url = (\n"
"    \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"    + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
")\n"
"headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n"
msgstr ""
"instance_url = (\n"
"    \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"    + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
")\n"
"headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(instance_url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(instance_url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `200 OK` response confirms that your token is valid. The current instance configuration is in the extensions field of the response. Use this instead of parameters, which might be stale.\n"
msgstr "Una risposta `200 OK` conferma che il tuo token è valido. La configurazione attuale dell'istanza si trova nel campo extensions della risposta. Usa questo campo invece di parameters, che potrebbe non essere aggiornato.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"step-3\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Look up the account-level functions configuration {#step-3-look-up-the-account-level-functions-configuration}"
msgstr "Passaggio 3: cercare la configurazione delle funzioni a livello di account {#step-3-look-up-the-account-level-functions-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An instance can only be granted access to what the account is entitled to. Before configuring the instance, look up the account's configuration so you know which functions, business models, and permissions are available to grant. This is the source of truth for the values you will send in Step 4.\n"
msgstr "A un'istanza può essere concesso l'accesso solo a ciò a cui l'account ha diritto. Prima di configurare l'istanza, cerca la configurazione dell'account in modo da sapere quali funzioni, modelli di business e permessi sono disponibili da concedere. Questa è la fonte autorevole per i valori che invierai nel Passaggio 4.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call `GET /accounts/{id}` on the Qiskit Runtime API with your API key. The `{id}` is your account ID without the `a/` prefix.  You can find it from the instance CRN (`crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...`).\n"
msgstr "Chiama `GET /accounts/{id}` sull'API Qiskit Runtime con la tua chiave API. `{id}` è l'ID del tuo account senza il prefisso `a/`. Puoi trovarlo dal CRN dell'istanza (`crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/<ACCOUNT_ID>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: apikey <YOUR_API_KEY>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"account_id = \"<ACCOUNT_ID>\"  # from the CRN: crn:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    f\"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/{account_id}\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\"},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"for plan in resp.json()[\"plans\"]:\n"
"    print(plan[\"plan_id\"], plan.get(\"functions\"), plan.get(\"custom_functions\"))\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    f\"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/{account_id}\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\"},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"for plan in resp.json()[\"plans\"]:\n"
"    print(plan[\"plan_id\"], plan.get(\"functions\"), plan.get(\"custom_functions\"))\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each plan in the response includes a functions array and, if configured, a `custom_functions` object. These list the exact name, provider, business model, and permissions values you can grant to an instance under that plan.\n"
msgstr "Ogni piano nella risposta include un array functions e, se configurato, un oggetto `custom_functions`. Questi elencano il nome esatto, il provider, il modello di business e i valori dei permessi che puoi concedere a un'istanza in quel piano.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"`GET /accounts/{id}` shows what is available to grant at the account level. `GET /functions` (see [Verify the result](#verify-result)) shows what a specific instance has already been granted. Use the **account** endpoint to discover valid values, and the **functions** endpoint to confirm the result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Configure functions access {#step-4-configure-functions-access}"
msgstr "Passaggio 4: configurare l'accesso alle funzioni {#step-4-configure-functions-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the instance to grant access to Catalog Functions and Custom Functions.\n"
msgstr "Aggiorna l'istanza per concedere l'accesso a Catalog Functions e Custom Functions.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important notes\">\n"
"- The `name`, `provider`, and `business_model` values in functions must exactly match entries configured at the account level (see the [previous step](#step-3)). Permissions must be a non-empty subset of the account's permissions for that function. Similarly, `custom_functions.permissions` must be a non-empty subset of the account's `custom_functions` permissions.\n"
"- Include a timestamp in parameters on every PATCH. The Resource Controller deduplicates PATCH requests by comparing incoming parameters to the last value it stored. If they match, the request is silently dropped with `200 OK` without reaching the service. Include a changing timestamp value to prevent this.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note importanti\">\n"
"- I valori `name`, `provider` e `business_model` nelle functions devono corrispondere esattamente alle voci configurate a livello di account (vedi il [passaggio precedente](#step-3)). I permessi devono essere un sottoinsieme non vuoto dei permessi dell'account per quella funzione. Analogamente, `custom_functions.permissions` deve essere un sottoinsieme non vuoto dei permessi `custom_functions` dell'account.\n"
"- Includi un timestamp in parameters a ogni PATCH. Resource Controller deduplica le richieste PATCH confrontando i parameters in arrivo con l'ultimo valore memorizzato. Se corrispondono, la richiesta viene scartata silenziosamente con `200 OK` senza raggiungere il servizio. Includi un valore di timestamp mutevole per evitarlo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request PATCH \\\n"
"  --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"  --data '{\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"      \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z\",\n"
"      \"functions\": [\n"
"        {\n"
"          \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"          \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"          \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"          \"permissions\": [\n"
"            \"function.read\",\n"
"            \"function.run\",\n"
"            \"function-files.read\",\n"
"            \"function-files.write\"\n"
"          ]\n"
"        }\n"
"      ],\n"
"      \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"        \"permissions\": [\n"
"          \"function-custom.write\",\n"
"          \"function-custom.run\"\n"
"        ]\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"from datetime import datetime, timezone\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "A changing timestamp keeps the Resource Controller from de-duplicating the request."
msgstr "Un timestamp mutevole impedisce a Resource Controller di deduplicare la richiesta."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n"
"timestamp = _now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{_now.microsecond:06d}000Z\"\n"
msgstr ""
"_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n"
"timestamp = _now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{_now.microsecond:06d}000Z\"\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body = {\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"        \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"        \"functions\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"                \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"                \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"                \"permissions\": [\n"
"                    \"function.read\",\n"
"                    \"function.run\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.read\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.write\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"            }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"            \"permissions\": [\"function-custom.write\", \"function-custom.run\"],\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"body = {\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"        \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"        \"functions\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"                \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"                \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"                \"permissions\": [\n"
"                    \"function.read\",\n"
"                    \"function.run\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.read\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.write\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"            }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"            \"permissions\": [\"function-custom.write\", \"function-custom.run\"],\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `200 OK` response indicates success. The updated configuration appears in the extensions field of the response.\n"
msgstr "Una risposta `200 OK` indica il successo. La configurazione aggiornata appare nel campo extensions della risposta.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove functions access {#remove-functions-access}"
msgstr "Rimuovere l'accesso alle funzioni {#remove-functions-access}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Catalog Functions {#catalog-functions}"
msgstr "Catalog Functions {#catalog-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove Catalog Functions from an instance, send a PATCH with `\"functions\": null`:\n"
msgstr "Per rimuovere Catalog Functions da un'istanza, invia una PATCH con `\"functions\": null`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"--data '{\n"
"  \"parameters\": {\n"
"    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:01Z\",\n"
"    \"functions\": null\n"
"  }\n"
"}'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"body = {\"parameters\": {\"timestamp\": timestamp, \"functions\": None}}\n"
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `\"functions\": []` (an empty array) equivalently clears Catalog Functions. `null` is the canonical form.\n"
msgstr "Impostare `\"functions\": []` (un array vuoto) cancella in modo equivalente Catalog Functions. `null` è la forma canonica.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom Functions {#custom-functions}"
msgstr "Custom Functions {#custom-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove Custom Functions from an instance, send a PATCH with `\"custom_functions\": null`:\n"
msgstr "Per rimuovere Custom Functions da un'istanza, invia una PATCH con `\"custom_functions\": null`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"--data '{\n"
"  \"parameters\": {\n"
"    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:02Z\",\n"
"    \"custom_functions\": null\n"
"  }\n"
"}'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"body = {\"parameters\": {\"timestamp\": timestamp, \"custom_functions\": None}}\n"
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `\"custom_functions\": {\"permissions\": []}` equivalently clears custom functions. `null` is the canonical form.\n"
msgstr "Impostare `\"custom_functions\": {\"permissions\": []}` cancella in modo equivalente le custom functions. `null` è la forma canonica.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-result\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the result {#verify-the-result}"
msgstr "Verificare il risultato {#verify-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To confirm that the instance has the correct Qiskit Functions configuration, use `GET /functions` from the Qiskit Runtime API instead of the Resource Controller. The Resource Controller's stored state might be stale if account-level changes updated the instance outside of the Resource Controller.\n"
msgstr "Per confermare che l'istanza abbia la configurazione corretta di Qiskit Functions, usa `GET /functions` dall'API Qiskit Runtime invece di Resource Controller. Lo stato memorizzato di Resource Controller potrebbe non essere aggiornato se modifiche a livello di account hanno aggiornato l'istanza al di fuori di Resource Controller.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: apikey <YOUR_API_KEY>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Service-CRN: <YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    ```python\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Service-CRN header takes the raw CRN, not the URL-encoded form."
msgstr "L'intestazione Service-CRN richiede il CRN grezzo, non la forma codificata per URL."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    \"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\", \"Service-CRN\": crn},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    \"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\", \"Service-CRN\": crn},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
